{"paper": "RRB-Technician-Grade-III-CBT-1-10-Mar-2026-Shift2.pdf", "status": "ok", "mode": "answer-anchored", "splitter": "qdot", "section_slice": true, "extracted_count": 25, "tagged_count": 25, "questions": [{"n": 1, "text": "Lalit deposits ₹42,000 in his account that pays an annual interest rate of 20% compounded half yearly. Calculate the total amount in his account after one year.", "options": [{"text": "₹50,820", "added": false}, {"text": "₹50,880", "added": false}, {"text": "₹50,650", "added": false}, {"text": "₹50,680 Question Type : MCQ", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Compound Interest", "sub": "compounding-frequency", "key_answer": "50820"}, {"n": 2, "text": "Three pipes X, Y, and Z can fill a tank in 12, 15, and 20 hours, respectively. All three pipes are opened together but pipe Z is closed 3 hours before the tank is completely filled. In how many hours will the tank be filled?", "options": [{"text": "6 hours 45 minutes", "added": false}, {"text": "5 hours 45 minutes", "added": false}, {"text": "6 hours 15 minutes", "added": false}, {"text": "5 hours 15 minutes Question Type : MCQ", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Pipes-Cisterns", "sub": "combined-pipes", "key_answer": "6"}, {"n": 3, "text": "A number when increased by 110%, gives 3570. The number is:6138", "options": [{"text": "5100", "added": false}, {"text": "3400", "added": false}, {"text": "1700", "added": false}, {"text": "850 Question Type : MCQ", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "increase-decrease", "key_answer": "1700"}, {"n": 4, "text": "One pipe can fill the tank in 14 min, while another pipe can empty the completely filled tank in 63 min. If both the pipes are operated together on empty tank, how long (in min) will it take to fill one-third of the tank?3939", "options": [{"text": "18", "added": false}, {"text": "24", "added": false}, {"text": "6